                <pb facs="0149" n="142" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg142"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/8707: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-07-12T16:00:00+08:00">July 12, 1937—4.
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 12—9:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>224. Embassy’s 223, July 12, 3 p.m.</p>
                <p>1. The Consul General at Tientsin has just telephoned that large numbers of
                    Japanese troops are arriving at intervals at East Station Tientsin and are going
                    into barracks at Tientsin. He states that the Shanghai express from the South
                    arrived at 1 p.m., today, stopped at West Station Tientsin, and will proceed no
                    further.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Nanking, Shanghai and Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
